<section>
  <grid spacing="none">
    <grid-item colspan="37" vertical-align="end" background-overlay="tint" background-overlay-intensity="0.46">
      <ai-image background="true" aspect-ratio="landscape" image-style="practical-light-afterimage" prompt="High-contrast overhead editorial studio photograph of anonymous hands interrupting a straight path of black paper with a small glass prism, one hard coral beam diverted into an amber trace with a faint ultraviolet residual afterimage, practical hard light, deep negative space around ordinary cutting and drawing tools, restrained grain, no faces, logos, text, or lettering"></ai-image>
      <p role="eyebrow">Deliberate variation</p>
      <h1>Design the interruption</h1>
      <p font-size="lg">Change one thing strongly enough to create evidence, not noise.</p>
    </grid-item>
    <grid-item colspan="23" background-color="surface" padding="38pt 32pt">
      <p role="eyebrow">Change one axis</p>
      <grid direction="vertical" spacing="small" vertical-sizing="fill">
        <grid-item cell-style="subtle">
          <h3>Material</h3>
          <p>Translate the idea into another medium.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item cell-style="subtle">
          <h3>Rule</h3>
          <p>Remove a familiar option or impose an unlikely limit.</p>
        </grid-item>
        <grid-item cell-style="subtle">
          <h3>Perspective</h3>
          <p>Let another discipline, audience, or scale reshape the question.</p>
        </grid-item>
      </grid>
      <p font-size="sm">One interruption at a time keeps the lesson visible.</p>
    </grid-item>
  </grid>
</section>